# UPSTREAM.sha256 -- every upstream byte this package carries, pinned.
#
# SHA-256 of EVERY regular file of the pinned GNU MP 6.3.0 release archive that
# this tree carries, unmodified, under its upstream path and under its upstream
# name. This file is the machine-checkable half of the record; UPSTREAM.md
# carries the prose, NOTICE.md the per-file licence terms.
# 2156 records, 16998222 bytes.
#
# 1. THE PIN
#
#   release             GNU MP 6.3.0
#   archive             gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz
#   primary URL         https://gmplib.org/download/gmp/gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz
#   mirror URL          https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gmp/gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz
#   archive SHA-256     a3c2b80201b89e68616f4ad30bc66aee4927c3ce50e33929ca819d5c43538898
#   archive size        2094196 bytes
#   top-level dir       gmp-6.3.0/
#   detached signature  gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz.sig, RSA key
#                       343C2FF0FBEE5EC2EDBEF399F3599FF828C67298 -- UNVERIFIED
#
#   The detached signature is UNVERIFIED and nothing in this record depends on
#   it. The GMP release key is not in the machine's keyring that produced this
#   record (`gpg --list-keys 343C2FF0FBEE5EC2EDBEF399F3599FF828C67298` reports
#   "No public key"), so the signature was never checked and no claim is made
#   about it. The archive digest above is the integrity anchor. Import the GMP
#   release key before relying on the signature; UPSTREAM.md records the same
#   fact and the same reason.
#
#   There is no upstream commit SHA to pin here and none is invented: GMP's
#   canonical SCM is Mercurial (https://gmplib.org/repo/gmp/) and this fork
#   imports a release archive, not a repository. Any GitHub mirror of GMP is a
#   mirror, not the canonical upstream. UPSTREAM.md states that in full.
#
# 2. HOW THE DIGESTS WERE DERIVED
#
#   2026-10-04, in a scratch directory outside this repository:
#
#     curl -fL -o gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz \
#       https://gmplib.org/download/gmp/gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz
#     sha256sum gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz
#       -> a3c2b80201b89e68616f4ad30bc66aee4927c3ce50e33929ca819d5c43538898
#          2094196 bytes, matching the pin above. The digest was checked BEFORE
#          the archive was opened; a mismatch would have stopped there and
#          nothing below would exist.
#     tar -xJf gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz    # exit 0; 2156 regular files, 186
#                                  # directories, 0 symlinks, 0 other entries
#     cd gmp-6.3.0
#     find . -type f -printf '%P\n' | LC_ALL=C sort > paths
#     sha256sum $(cat paths) > manifest
#
#   Every digest below was measured from the freshly extracted upstream tree and
#   never from this working tree, so this record is a pin and not a description
#   of whatever the checkout happens to hold. The path set comes from the
#   archive's own file list, not from a walk of this repository, so a
#   fork-authored file cannot enter the record by accident.
#
#   The tool was GNU coreutils sha256sum 9.6 (`/usr/bin/sha256sum --version`),
#   reading raw file bytes: no text normalisation, no EOL translation, no
#   filtering, no archive metadata, no git. Each digest was computed twice, once
#   with `/usr/bin/sha256sum` and once with the hashing tool this session
#   resolves by bare name; the two manifests were byte identical, and the four
#   licence digests they produce are the four UPSTREAM.md has always published.
#   Paths are listed in LC_ALL=C byte order. No path of this tree was hashed to
#   produce this record; only the extracted upstream archive was.
#
#   The record was then verified against this checkout, from the repository
#   root:
#
#     sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256
#
#   2156 records, 2156 OK, 0 FAILED, 0 recorded paths missing. Comparing the
#   extracted archive's own 2156-path file list against this record gives 0
#   upstream paths missing from the record and 0 recorded paths missing from the
#   tree. Every regular file of gmp-6.3.0/ is present here, at its upstream
#   path, at the archive's own bytes. There is no divergence to report.
#
# 3. THE PATH SET: 2156 records
#
#   The whole archive, filtered by nothing. This is deliberately a superset of
#   what this build compiles, reads, installs or publishes terms for: upstream
#   build files, upstream's own test suite, the demos, the tuning programs, the
#   alternate mini-gmp implementation, the C++ interface and every tuned
#   assembly directory are retained as material, so they are recorded here
#   rather than dropped from the record.
#
#   1341  mpn/                      the low-level layer
#         190  mpn/generic/         188 .c plus gmp-mparam.h and hgcd2-div.h:
#                                    the portable C backend this graph compiles
#         1144  mpn/<cpu>/          27 tuned-assembly directories, imported but
#                                    never compiled here (this build selects the
#                                    portable C backend with NO_ASM 1):
#                                    x86_64 314, x86 215, powerpc64 78, arm 75,
#                                    sparc64 61, alpha 49, powerpc32 40,
#                                    arm64 39, sparc32 37, s390_64 35, ia64 32,
#                                    pa32 25, cray 21, s390_32 21, loongarch 12,
#                                    pa64 12, m68k 11, mips32 11, mips64 11,
#                                    power 10, riscv 9, vax 9, m88k 8, sh 5,
#                                    thumb 2, lisp 1, minithres 1
#            7  mpn/ top level       Makefile.am, Makefile.in, Makeasm.am,
#                                    asm-defs.m4, README, cpp-ccas, m4-ccas
#    251  tests/                    upstream's own test suite: 202 .c, 22 .cc,
#                                    3 .asm, tests/tests.h and 4 further .h,
#                                    9 Makefile.am and 9 Makefile.in for
#                                    tests/{cxx,devel,misc,mpf,mpn,mpq,mpz,rand},
#                                    tests/devel/README. GMP ships its test
#                                    inputs as the programs themselves; upstream
#                                    has no separate testdata directory, so none
#                                    is missing here
#    166  mpz/                       integers
#     61  tune/                      tuning programs: imported, not built
#     61  root-level files           see the breakdown below
#     47  demos/                     example programs: imported, not built
#     45  mini-gmp/                  the alternate single-file implementation:
#                                    imported, not built
#     34  mpq/                       rationals
#     23  printf/                    formatted output
#     16  rand/                      pseudorandom numbers
#     15  doc/                       the manual: gmp.texi, fdl-1.3.texi,
#                                    texinfo.tex, version.texi, configuration,
#                                    isa_abi_headache, mdate-sh, projects.html,
#                                    tasks.html, gmp.info, gmp.info-1,
#                                    gmp.info-2, stamp-vti, Makefile.am,
#                                    Makefile.in
#     14  cxx/                       the C++ interface for libgmpxx: imported,
#                                    not built, because this graph builds only
#                                    libgmp
#     11  scanf/                     formatted input
#   ----
#   2156  total
#
#   The 61 root-level files, which is the rest of the record:
#
#     26  library sources and table generators: assert.c, bootstrap.c,
#          compat.c, errno.c, extract-dbl.c, gen-bases.c, gen-fac.c, gen-fib.c,
#          gen-jacobitab.c, gen-psqr.c, gen-sieve.c, gen-trialdivtab.c,
#          invalid.c, memory.c, mp_bpl.c, mp_clz_tab.c, mp_dv_tab.c,
#          mp_get_fns.c, mp_minv_tab.c, mp_set_fns.c, nextprime.c,
#          primesieve.c, tal-debug.c, tal-notreent.c, tal-reent.c, version.c
#      4  public and internal headers: asl.h, gmp-impl.h, gmpxx.h, longlong.h
#      4  configuration and packaging templates: config.in, gmp-h.in,
#          gmp.pc.in, gmpxx.pc.in
#      2  the top-level build files: Makefile.am, Makefile.in
#     14  autotools scaffolding: acinclude.m4, aclocal.m4, compile,
#          config.guess, config.sub, configfsf.guess, configfsf.sub, configure,
#          configure.ac, install-sh, ltmain.sh, missing, test-driver, ylwrap
#      4  the licence texts: COPYING, COPYING.LESSERv3, COPYINGv2, COPYINGv3
#      7  upstream's own prose, history and debugging setup: AUTHORS,
#          ChangeLog, INSTALL, INSTALL.autoconf, NEWS, README, .gdbinit
#   ----
#     61  total
#
#   23 Makefile.am and 23 Makefile.in files are inside the directory counts
#   above, one pair per recursive directory (mpn, mpz, mpq, mpf, printf, scanf,
#   rand, cxx, doc, tune, mini-gmp and the eight tests/ subdirectories). They
#   are build files this fork never invokes, and they are recorded because
#   upstream shipped them.
#
# 4. WHAT IS RECORDED THAT IS NOT COMPILED
#
#   503 of the 2156 records are C translation units this build compiles: the 498
#   entries of `all` in zig/sources.zig plus the 5 distinct multi-function
#   templates `operations` instantiates once per operation
#   (mpn/generic/popham.c, sec_div.c, sec_pi1_div.c, sec_aors_1.c,
#   logops_n.c). Every one of those 503 is in this record at its upstream
#   digest.
#
#   The other 1653 records are material this package retains and does not
#   compile: the 5 files under mpn/generic/ that this build does not compile
#   (div_qr_1n_pi2.c, div_qr_1u_pi2.c, udiv_w_sdiv.c, gmp-mparam.h,
#   hgcd2-div.h -- the first three are upstream's own tuning alternatives and
#   the fourth and fifth are headers the selected translation units do not
#   include), all 1144 tuned assembly files, upstream's own test suite, the
#   demos, the tuning programs, mini-gmp, the C++ interface, the autotools
#   scaffolding, the manual, and the licence and history files. They are
#   recorded anyway, because an edit to any of them is still an edit to
#   upstream's bytes.
#
#   Two files that upstream generates are correctly ABSENT from this record,
#   because they are not upstream bytes and are not in this tree:
#   mpn/fib_table.c and mpn/mp_bases.c. They are produced at build time by the
#   upstream table generators gen-fib.c and gen-bases.c, which ARE records here,
#   and are written to the Zig cache directory, never into the source tree
#   (.gitignore excludes them). The same holds for the generated headers
#   gmp.h, config.h, mpn/gmp-mparam.h and the pkg-config files: their upstream
#   TEMPLATES -- gmp-h.in, config.in, mpn/generic/gmp-mparam.h, gmp.pc.in,
#   gmpxx.pc.in -- are all records here.
#
# 5. DELIBERATELY ABSENT, EACH FOR A STATED REASON
#
#   UPSTREAM.sha256        this file: a record cannot contain its own digest.
#                         It is protected by tools/provenance_gate.sh, which
#                         fails if it is missing, empty, shrunk, or if any line
#                         of it stops being a digest record.
#   README.upstream.md    NOT upstream's path. Upstream ships its README as
#                         `README`, which is carried here at its upstream name
#                         and IS a record. README.upstream.md is this fork's
#                         own byte-identical copy of it, kept so the fork can
#                         have a README.md of its own without overwriting the
#                         upstream text. The gate checks both files against the
#                         same digest.
#   the fork's own files, 49, none of which is upstream's:
#                         .envrc, .github/workflows/ci.yml, .gitignore,
#                         CHANGELOG.md, FORK-LICENSE.md, FORK-NOTES.md,
#                         NOTICE.md, README.md, README.upstream.md,
#                         README.zig.md, UPSTREAM.md, build.zig, build.zig.zon,
#                         consumer/build.zig, consumer/build.zig.zon,
#                         consumer/src/main.zig, devenv.nix, devenv.yaml,
#                         flake.nix, include/gmp_all.h, package.nix, root.zig,
#                         runtime/generate.zig, runtime/graph.zig,
#                         runtime/library.zig, runtime/loader.zig,
#                         runtime/sync.c, runtime/sync.h,
#                         tools/provenance_gate.sh, zig/BigInt.zig,
#                         zig/Float.zig, zig/Rand.zig, zig/Rational.zig,
#                         zig/api_exercise.zig, zig/base.zig, zig/config_gen.zig,
#                         zig/example/main.zig, zig/memory.zig, zig/provider.zig,
#                         zig/sources.zig, zig/test/alloc_probe.c,
#                         zig/test/alloc_probe.zig, zig/test/bootstrap.zig,
#                         zig/test/division.zig, zig/test/known_answers.zig,
#                         zig/test/ownership.zig, zig/test/parsing.zig,
#                         zig/test/rational_float_random.zig, zig/test/root.zig
#
#   .gitignore deserves its own note because it is the one file sibling forks
#   carry an edited copy of and here there is nothing to edit: gmp-6.3.0 ships
#   NO .gitignore at all. It is absent from the archive's 2156-path file list,
#   so there is no upstream digest for it and no deviation to record. The 51-line
#   file this repository carries is entirely this fork's, and it is one of the
#   49 above. (`.gdbinit` at the root IS upstream's and IS a record.)
#
#   build outputs         `.zig-cache/`, `zig-out/`, `consumer/zig-out/` and the
#                         files listed in .gitignore's generated-file section.
#                         They are not in this repository and are not upstream's.
#
# 6. RE-DERIVING AND RE-CHECKING
#
#   Re-check, from the repository root, with no network, no compiler and no
#   build -- this is what CI runs first:
#
#     sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256          # or: sh tools/provenance_gate.sh .
#
#   Re-derive, in a scratch directory outside this repository, from the pin in
#   section 1:
#
#     curl -fL -o gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz \
#       https://gmplib.org/download/gmp/gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz
#     sha256sum gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz     # must equal the pin, before extracting
#     tar -xJf gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz
#     cd gmp-6.3.0
#     find . -type f -printf '%P\n' | LC_ALL=C sort \
#       | xargs sha256sum > ../manifest
#     cd ..
#     grep -v '^#' UPSTREAM.sha256 | LC_ALL=C sort > pinned
#     LC_ALL=C sort manifest -o manifest
#     diff manifest pinned
#
#   A clean diff is the whole claim: this record is the pinned archive, file for
#   file. Anything the archive carries and this record does not, and any digest
#   that differs, is a finding to report, never a line to rewrite.
#
#   What this record is not: it is not tamper evidence against someone who edits
#   a native file AND rewrites that file's line here, because a manifest cannot
#   contain the digest of the thing it is supposed to police. What it does make
#   expensive and loud is the ordinary case -- an edited source, a deleted test,
#   a renamed path, a dropped record, a stale licence text -- and what section 6
#   above makes checkable is the only claim that matters: these 2156 lines were
#   derived from the pinned archive, and re-deriving them from the archive again
#   reproduces them exactly. The archive digest in section 1 is what a reader
#   re-downloads; if a line here ever stops matching that archive, the archive
#   is right and the line is wrong.
